WHY THIS LICENCE AND NOT ANOTHER
--------------------------------

These crates are compiled into both Girsa and Ksav. Ksav is MIT OR Apache-2.0,
so this repository has to be too — a copyleft dependency here would relicense
both applications through the shared code.

That is not an abstract concern. Three projects in this problem space are
directly relevant prior art and all three are copyleft:

  * Zayit .................... AGPL-3.0 with a Section 7b additional term
  * HebMorph ................. AGPL
  * Sefaria-ElasticSearch .... GPL-3.0

They may be read to understand the problem. No code, table, word list or data
file from any of them may be copied into this repository, in whole or in part.
Behaviour described in prose may be reimplemented from scratch; a prefix table
lifted verbatim is a licence violation regardless of how small it is.

Otzaria is UNLICENSE (public domain) and is safe to draw from.
